\ Local-accumulate fusion: `<value> acc <fop> to acc` folds into one op that
\ reads-modifies-writes the local accumulator (acc = value <op> acc). Covers
\ depth-0 locals and depth-1 (an enclosing scope's local used inside a
\ quotation), for f+ f- f* f/. Values must match the unfused sequence.

\ depth 0
: a0 0 to acc 1 acc f+ to acc 2 acc f+ to acc 3 acc f+ to acc acc ;
a0 . cr                       \ 0->1->3->6

: m0 1 to acc 2 acc f* to acc 3 acc f* to acc 4 acc f* to acc acc ;
m0 . cr                       \ 1->2->6->24

: s0 2 to acc 5 acc f- to acc 10 acc f- to acc acc ;
s0 . cr                       \ value - acc: 2->3->7

: d0 2 to acc 12 acc f/ to acc 18 acc f/ to acc acc ;
d0 . cr                       \ value / acc: 2->6->3

\ an enclosing scope's accumulator is out of reach from a quotation, so the fold
\ carries it on the stack instead — which is what reduce is for
: q1  5 iota 0 ' + reduce ;
q1 . cr                       \ sum 0..4 = 10

: q2  4 iota 1 [: product i | i 1+ product * :] reduce ;
q2 . cr                       \ 1*2*3*4 = 24

clear
\ === errors ===
